Putting it another way:

Wearing an amulet of life saving is inherently useless unless you
actually die. If you ascend while wearing an amulet of life saving,
it's proof that you've been wasting your amulet slot when you could
have had something much more useful there.

Whereas, if you *do* die while wearing an amulet of life saving, then
when you revive *you are in the presence of something that's already
shown it's good enough to kill you*. The major likelihood is that
you'll simply get killed again by the same thing in short order -
death by running SLOWLY out of hit points is unlikely, at the kind of
time in the game where you are likely to actually have a "oLS, so the
chances are that whatever killed you was either an instadeath that
didn't depend on your hit points (e.g. stoning, sickness), or
something that could take off a LARGE chunk of your hps very fast. In
either case you're still standing right beside it, with no more
protection than you had last time when it killed you...

